axes.runtime:
An official hosted remote server (mcp.datadoghq.com/v1/mcp — direct fetch 401 = exists, auth required);
there is also a local-binary line (the coterm.datadoghq.com install script installs datadog_mcp_cli, stdio connecting to remote tools).
The official docs state plainly **not GovCloud compatible**; HIPAA-eligible.

axes.local_files:
Never touches the local file system — the scope is Datadog cloud data.
Exception: the official docs carry a **separate Code Security MCP Server** (running SAST/SCA/IaC/secrets/SBOM scans locally);
the docs say explicitly it is a narrow, separate line, not the subject of this entry.

mcp.transport:
**Streamable HTTP** (remote https://mcp.datadoghq.com/v1/mcp) is primary;
the local binary datadog_mcp_cli uses stdio (authentication happens locally, tools remain remote).
Verified against: the official docs setup page (direct-fetched 2026-10-23).

mcp.auth:
OAuth 2.0 (recommended, clients run the flow automatically; custom subdomains need a ?subdomain= parameter);
or a PAT/SAT Bearer header; or DD_API_KEY + DD_APPLICATION_KEY headers (the official docs recommend a scoped service-account key).
The endpoint's direct-fetch 401 = exists, auth required.
